[13] 1. Confidential Information. 

[14] The term “Confidential Information” means any and all tangible and intangible information disclosed to Receiver in any medium or form relating to VIDAR’s products, design, engineering, research, development, software, marketing, manufacturing processes, pricing, business plans, and any other information concerning VIDAR’s business and goodwill, including without limitation, plans, know-how, computer programs, software, algorithms, techniques, methodologies, designs, drawings, analyses, evaluations, formulations, samples, processes, machines, prototypes, product performance data, proposals, job notes, reports, records, specifications, manuals, supplier and customer lists and information, licenses, prices for licensing software products and services, purchase and sales records, marketing information, or any other information which is identified as being of a confidential or proprietary nature or should be considered confidential under the circumstances.

[16] Receiver shall:

[17] (i) hold the Confidential Information in strict confidence;

[18] (ii) use the Confidential Information only for the purposes as expressly directed by VIDAR;

[19] (iii) provide such information only to those of its personnel who: 

[20] (y) have a need to know the same to further VIDAR’s interests; and 

[21] (z) become a party to and bound by a confidentiality agreement at least as restrictive as this Agreement prior to receiving any such information.

[22] Receiver will not disclose Confidential Information to any party who do not meet the preceding requirements.

[24] 3. Additional Disclosures. 

[25] Receiver may disclose Confidential Information if the same:

[26] (a) was generally available at the time it was disclosed other than as a result of a disclosure made by Receiver;

[27] (b) was known to the Receiver at the time it received such information, as evidenced by contemporaneous documentation in Receiver’s files;

[28] (c) is disclosed with the prior written approval of VIDAR;

[29] (d) becomes known to Receiver on a non-confidential basis from a source other than VIDAR without breach of this Agreement by Receiver;

[30] (e) is disclosed to a third party by VIDAR without restrictions against non-disclosure similar to those contained in this Agreement;

[31] (f) is disclosed pursuant to the order or requirement of a court; administrative agency, or other government body, provided Receiver takes all reasonable steps to keep the Confidential Information from becoming part of public records; or

[32] (g) is hereafter independently developed by Receiver without the aid, application or use of any Confidential Information;

[33] provided for each that: 

[34] (i) Receiver promptly notifies VIDAR of such action; and 

[35] (ii) in any action to enforce or remedy a breach of this Agreement, Receiver shall have the burden of establishing the applicability of the subsection on which it relies.

[49] Upon the request of VIDAR or the termination or expiration of this Confidential Agreement, Receiver shall promptly return to VIDAR all copies of the Confidential Information and obtained by Receiver.

[50] 7. Disclaimer. 

[51] Receiver acknowledges that the Confidential Information may relate to processes or products that are developmental and may or may not have been reduced to practical application in prototype form.

[52] Accordingly, Receiver understands that neither VIDAR has made or makes any representation or warranty as to the accuracy, completeness or value of the Confidential Information.

[54] 8. Injunction. 

[55] Receiver acknowledges and agrees that:

[56] (i) the Confidential Information is proprietary to and valuable information of VIDAR;

[57] (ii) VIDAR derives economic value from the Confidential Information not being generally known to other persons who can obtain economic value from its disclosure or use;

[58] (iii) any disclosure or unauthorized use of the Confidential Information could cause irreparable harm and loss to VIDAR;

[59] (iv) if this Agreement is breached, VIDAR can not be made whole by monetary damages.

[60] Accordingly, VIDAR, in addition to any other remedy to which it may be entitled by law or in equity, shall be entitled to an injunction to prevent further breaches of this Agreement and to an order compelling specific performance of this Agreement.

[61] Receiver shall reimburse VIDAR for all costs and expenses, including attorney’s fees, incurred by VIDAR in enforcing the obligations of Receiver.

[66] VIDAR may terminate this Agreement at any time for any reason.

[67] 9. General. 

[69] This Agreement contains the entire understanding and agreement of the parties hereto with respect to the subject matter contained herein, supersedes all prior oral or written understandings and agreements relating thereto, except as expressly otherwise provided, and may not be altered, modified or waived in whole or in part, except in writing, signed by duly authorized representatives of the parties hereto.

