text:
[1] NON-DISCLOSURE AGREEMENT

[2] R 2019/01

[26] Information means information relating to one party made available by such party to the other party for the Business Purpose, excluding:

[27] I. information that is publicly available or becomes publicly available (other than as a result of disclosure by the Receiving Party or any other person contrary to the terms of this Agreement);

[28] II. information available to the Receiving Party or another person to whom it is furnished free of any restriction as to its use or disclosure prior to its being so furnished;

[29] III. information available to the Receiving Party from a source other than the Disclosing Party, which source is not bound by any obligation of confidentiality to the Disclosing Party in relation to such Information;

[30] IV. information independently developed by the Receiving Party;

[31] V. information required to be disclosed, retained or maintained by law or any regulation or any governmental organization.

[32] Confidential Information may also be handed out by a third party appointed by the Disclosing Party (i.e., manufacturer).

[34] I. treat the Information with the same degree of care to avoid disclosure to any third party as is used with respect to the Receiving Party's own Information of like importance which is to be kept confidential;

[35] II. keep the Information relating to the other party secret and confidential and not disclose any of it to any third person and only make it available to the Receiving Party's executive board, directors, employees, advisers, or subsidiaries who need to know the same for the Business Purpose;

[36] III. use the Information only for the Business Purpose unless the Disclosing Party gives its prior written consent to such Information being used for some other agreed purpose;

[37] IV. keep the Information, relating to the Disclosing Party, and any copies thereof secure and in such a way as to prevent unauthorized access by any third party, nor make any copies of it or reproduce it in any form;

[38] V. ensure that its employees and advisers comply with the obligations of non-disclosure arising from this Agreement.

[40] All Information exchanged between the Parties pursuant to this Agreement shall upon request of the Disclosing Party either be returned to the Disclosing Party or be destroyed. On request, the Receiving Party shall supply a written certificate signed by any of its directors confirming the destruction of the Information.

[43] The Information relating to the other party shall remain the property of such other party (as Disclosing Party) and its disclosure shall not confer on the other party (as Receiving Party) any rights.

[46] The Agreement shall continue in force for three years from the signing of this Agreement. Thereafter, it shall automatically continue unless terminated upon thirty days prior notice in writing. The obligations accruing prior to termination as set forth herein shall, however, survive the termination of this Agreement for a period of two years.

[48] The Agreement shall be governed and construed by the laws of Singapore, without regard to any conflict of law principles leading to the application of the laws of any other jurisdiction. The Parties hereby submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Singapore.

[52] The provisions of this Agreement may not be modified, amended, nor waived, except by a written instrument duly executed by the Parties hereto. The requirement of written form can only be waived in writing.

[54] This Agreement may not be assigned by either party without the prior written consent of the other.

[55] Insofar as one of the Parties undergoes a transformation by change in its legal form preserving its identity or by a change in legal personality due to merger, break up, or transfer of assets, this Agreement shall be continued with the newly formed legal successor or the legal successor taking over one of the Parties.

Singapore, Date Place, Date

Holger Roessner, Signatory Name

AdvanIDe Europe GmbH &

AdvanIDe Holdings Pte Ltd &

AdvanIDe Americas, Inc

