[14] The Receiving Party agrees to:

[15] (a) Receive and maintain the Confidential Information in confidence;

[16] (b) Not reproduce the Confidential Information or any part thereof without the express written consent of Disclosing Party;

[17] (c) Not, directly or indirectly, make known, divulge, publish or communicate the Confidential Information to any person, firm or corporation without the express written consent of Disclosing Party;

[18] (d) Limit the internal dissemination of the Confidential Information and the internal disclosure of the Confidential Information received from the Disclosing Party to those officers and employees, if any, of the Receiving Party who have a need to know and an obligation to protect it;

[19] (e) Not use or utilize the Confidential Information without the express written consent of Disclosing Party;

[20] (f) Not use the Confidential Information or any part thereof as a basis for the design or creation of any method, system, apparatus or device similar to any method, system, apparatus or device embodied in the Confidential Information unless expressly authorized in writing by Disclosing Party;

[21] (g) Utilize the best efforts possible to protect and safeguard the Confidential Information from loss, theft, destruction, or the like;

[22] (h) Not reverse engineer any objects which embody Disclosing Party's Confidential Information;

[23] (i) Not solicit some of Disclosing Party's representatives;

[24] (j) Not disclose the fact that Agreement was agreed or negotiated;

[25] (k) Not acquire information similar to Confidential Information from a third party;

[26] (l) Not share some Confidential Information with some third-parties (including consultants, agents and professional advisors) without the express written consent of Disclosing Party;

[27] (m) Not share some Confidential Information with some of Receiving Party's employees without the express written consent of Disclosing Party;

[28] (n) Not independently develop information similar to Confidential Information;

[29] (o) Not retain some Confidential Information even after the return or destruction of Confidential Information;

[30] (p) Not destroy or return some Confidential Information upon the termination of Agreement;

[31] (q) Not use any Confidential Information for any purpose other than the purposes stated in Agreement.

[24] 3. RETURN OF CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION

[25] All information provided by the Disclosing Party shall remain the property of the Disclosing Party. 

[26] Receiving Party agrees to return all Confidential Information to Disclosing Party within 15 days of written demand by Disclosing Party. 

[27] When the Receiving Party has finished reviewing the information provided by the Disclosing Party and has made a decision as to whether or not to work with the Disclosing Party, Receiving Party shall return all information to the Disclosing Party without retaining any copies.

[36] 6. NO LICENSE

[37] This agreement shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the parties hereto and their respective heirs, personal representatives, successors and assigns.

[44] Any controversy or claim arising out of or relating to this agreement, or the breach thereof, shall be resolved by arbitration conducted by the Commercial Division of the American Arbitration Association and in accordance with the rules thereof, or in any other convenient forum agreed to in writing by the parties. 

[45] Any arbitration award shall be final and binding, and judgment upon the award rendered pursuant to such arbitration may be entered in any court of proper jurisdiction. 

[46] Notwithstanding the foregoing, either party may seek and obtain temporary injunctive relief from any court of competent jurisdiction against any improper disclosure of the Confidential Information.

