[4] The Agreement is valid from the moment the authorized representative of the Company clicks "Sign Non-Disclosure Agreement" at PromonLogicalis’ website.

[5] The Agreement aims to ensure the confidentiality of information disclosed by one Party (the “Disclosing Party”) to the other (the “Receiving Party”) during any evaluation, negotiations, or commercial relationship.

[11] Confidential Information includes all written and verbal information marked as confidential or identified as such by the Disclosing Party, including trade secrets, discoveries, ideas, know-how, techniques, technology, products, designs, specifications, drawings, data, computer programs, business activities, reports, studies, and other technical, commercial, and financial information.

[15] The Receiving Party agrees to keep all Confidential Information confidential for the period specified in Section 13, and to restrict disclosure to the minimum number of people necessary, direct its employees, agents, and subcontractors to maintain confidentiality, and take proper measures to protect the secrecy of the Confidential Information.

[22] The Receiving Party shall:

[23] a. Restrict disclosure to the minimum number of people necessary;
[24] b. Direct its employees, agents, and subcontractors to maintain confidentiality;
[25] c. Use the same degree of care to protect the Confidential Information as it uses to protect its own confidential information, but at least commercially reasonable care;
[26] d. Notify the Disclosing Party of any misappropriation or misuse of Confidential Information.

[27] Breach of the terms of this Agreement may result in:

[28] a. Termination of any agreement between the Parties without compensation, with the breaching party liable for penalties for breach of contract;
[29] b. Payment of damages as set forth in Section 9 and applicable law.

[31] Confidential Information shall not include:

[32] a. Information already known to the Receiving Party in a legal and legitimate manner;
[33] b. Information for which the Disclosing Party has given prior written consent to release the obligation of secrecy and confidentiality;
[34] c. Information lawfully obtained by the Receiving Party from a third party without restrictions as to use and disclosure;
[35] d. Information disclosed by a court order, provided the Receiving Party promptly notifies the Disclosing Party and cooperates to prevent such disclosure;
[36] e. Publicly available information;
[37] f. Information independently developed by or for the Receiving Party.

[41] All Confidential Information shall remain the property of the Disclosing Party and shall be returned to it or destroyed promptly at its request.

[46] The Disclosing Party shall recover any and all damages in case of breach of any obligation by the Receiving Party, without liability for indirect damages or loss of profits.

[49] The Disclosing Party may seek injunctive relief to prevent unauthorized disclosure or use of Confidential Information without proving actual damages.

[50] Any third party owner of the disclosed information shall be an intended third party beneficiary of this Agreement and may rely on and directly enforce the terms and conditions hereof.

[52] The execution of this Agreement shall not be construed as granting any Party or its representatives any license or right to use any Confidential Information for its own benefit or the benefit of any other person, firm, or entity.

[53] The disclosure of confidential information is not a commitment to enter into any business arrangement.

[56] The Agreement shall be in force on the Execution Date and shall remain in force for a period of twenty-four (24) months, with the confidentiality obligation extending for three (3) years after the disclosure of Confidential Information.

